# Every testnet working directory, present and future. Enumerating them by name
# is how .testnet3/ got committed one commit after .testnet2/ was removed for
# carrying member secret keys: the rule was correct and the next directory was
# simply not in it. A working directory holds members.json, so the glob is the
# only version of this rule that stays true.
/.testnet*/
/.wallet/
/_external/

